@title A placed circuit lands where the pointer was on the drawing
@area Schematic
@sizes 1366x768
# Test report 16: circuits dropped at a fixed top-left spot, not at the cursor.
# Rule (macro_place::origin_in_view): the top-left of the circuit's box (symbol origins and pins, plus 15 mm for a
# symbol's body and tag text on every side) goes to the point where the pointer last rested on the drawing, snapped
# to the grid, then kept on the sheet: x at most sheet width - box width - 10 mm, y at most sheet height - box height - 10 mm
# (50 mm when the box reaches into the title block's 150 mm), both at least 10 mm.
# Both spots are chosen far from those limits, so nothing is clamped and the two pictures differ by exactly the
# distance between the spots. The status bar reads the pointer in mm only while it is over the drawing: the click on the
# Place button moves it off, so each scenario moves it back to the spot before the picture (a cross shows it).
click_text "New project"
wait 20
move 300 110
wait 5
key ctrl+k
text "start/stop latch"
wait 5
key Enter
wait 10
try click_text "Start/stop latch" Label
wait 10
click_text Place Button
wait 20
expect "Placed Start/stop latch"
move 300 110
wait 5
shot first-spot-300-110
move 700 110
wait 5
key ctrl+k
text "start/stop latch"
wait 5
key Enter
wait 10
try click_text "Start/stop latch" Label
wait 10
click_text Place Button
wait 20
expect "Placed Start/stop latch"
move 700 110
wait 5
shot second-spot-700-110
